  "created": "2022-08-09T02:12:26.774Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When hiding an avatar through the distance feature it causes physics joints with no connected body such as fixed joints or spring joints to offset themselves based on the movement the player is making while they are hidden. This also causes any components on children of the object with the joint to gain the same offset rather than being located where they are intended to be once they are shown again. This causes things like contacts or physbones to be offset based on the distance and direction the player being hidden was moving in.\nTo work around this issue, assuming the joint has the option, the player must disable \"auto configure connected anchor\". Not all joints have this option and would require switching to a joint that does to hopefully achieve the users desired effect.",
